Scoring and Decision Approach: Not addressed in this paper.
Results: *   252 feasibility questionnaires were received over a 6-yea
r period.
*   207 questionnaires were accepted and 45 were rejected.
*   Reasons for rejections: inappropriate therapeutic area (44%), comp
eting studies (31%), pharmaceutical company/CRO delay (13%), and other
 (12%).
*   An average of 26.8% of accepted feasibilities resulted in trials s
tarting.
*   Pharmaceutical companies consistently initiated more trials that r
esulted in patient enrolment than CROs.
*   The average time from feasibility acceptance to patient enrolment 
was 12.9 months (range 2.7–33.5 months).
Findings: *   A total of 252 feasibility questionnaires were received 
over a 6-year period.
*   207 questionnaires were accepted, and 45 were rejected.
*   The average percentage of trials started from accepted feasibiliti
es was 26.8%.
*   Pharmaceutical companies consistently initiated more trials that r
esulted in patient enrolment compared to CROs.
*   The average time from feasibility acceptance to first patient enro
lment was 12.9 months, ranging from 2.7 to 33.5 months.
