AB  - Background Careful site selection methods and tools such as questionna
ires have evolved to become “best” practice in the commercial and non-
commercial clinical trials setting. However, there is little evidence 
in the literature of the value of such methodology on trial delivery a
nd there is no generally acceptable model or tool available for use in
 site selection. The Nottingham Clinical Trials Unit introduced a site
 selection questionnaire in 2010, consisting of both generic research 
related questions and study specific protocol driven requirements for 
identification of potential sites in four multi-centre trials. Initial
ly questionnaires were sent to Principal Investigators at sites who ha
d expressed an interest in participating in the trials.
