AB  - This paper studies the feasibility of playing a First Person Shooter i
nteractive online game while traveling as a passenger on a car in an u
rban scenario where wireless connectivity is available through WiFi Ac
cess Points (APs). Knowing in advance the positions of APs, we propose
 a mechanism that is capable of predicting future connectivity times w
hile moving, so that a player may choose (or not) to begin a game roun
d. With such estimation of connectivity time, a player can obtain a fe
eling regarding which parts of a game s/he could (not) accomplish and 
hence be put in the position of deciding for the best. We validated ou
r approach through simulations utilizing a large set of real vehicular
 movement traces collected in Pisa, Italy.
